module

public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Modules.IdealSubsheafLocal
public import StacksFrontier.Homology.DerivedComplete.ConstantTowerProVanishing
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.GlobalSectionSmul
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Center.Shift
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Homology.DerivedCategory.FullyFaithful

/-!
# The morphisms out of the tower of ideal powers into an annihilated sheaf pro-vanish

Let `(C, J)` be a site, `O` a sheaf of commutative rings on it and `I ⊆ O` a sheaf of ideals.
The positive powers of `I` form an inverse system

`Stacks.Sites.idealPowTower I : ℕᵒᵖ ⥤ SheafOfModules O`, `m ↦ Iᵐ⁺¹`,

the transition maps being the inclusions. This file proves that the morphisms out of that system
into a sheaf of modules `F` killed by `Iᴺ` pro-vanish in the sense of
`NoetherianAdicCompletion.HomProVanishing`: every morphism `Iᵐ⁺¹ ⟶ F` is annihilated by a
transition map, and in fact by the one from level `N + m`, which is the first level at which the
bound can be taken uniformly in the morphism. Equivalently
`colim_m Hom(Iᵐ⁺¹, F) = 0`.

The same statement holds for the tower read in the derived category through
`CategoryTheory.DerivedCategory.singleFunctor`, with `F` placed in degree zero. That is
`Stacks.Sites.homProVanishing_idealPowTower_singleFunctor`, and it is the degree-zero case of the
derived vanishing `colim_m Ext^j(Iᵐ⁺¹, F) = 0` that the constant-tower criterion of
`Homology/DerivedComplete/ConstantTowerProVanishing.lean` consumes. Only degree zero is proved
here, and `Stacks.Sites.homProVanishing_idealPowTower` is the whole of it: in the derived category
of sheaves on a site `Hom(O, F⟦j⟧)` is the cohomology `H^j(F)`, which need not vanish for
`j ≥ 1`, so the long exact sequence of `Iᵐ⁺¹ ⟶ O ⟶ O/Iᵐ⁺¹` does not reduce the higher degrees to
the degree-zero statement the way it does over a ring, where `O` is free. See the implementation
notes.

The degree-zero case is nevertheless everything the dévissage needs **except** the higher `Ext`:
`Stacks.Sites.homProVanishing_idealPowTower_singleFunctor_of_isGE_of_isLE` runs the
truncation-restricted dévissage of
`NoetherianAdicCompletion.homProVanishing_of_isGE_of_isLE_of_mem_of_isLE` at the tower, for a
target with bounded cohomology annihilated by a family of central elements, and is left with the
single hypothesis `colim_m Ext^j(Iᵐ⁺¹, F) = 0` for `j ≥ 1`. The degrees `j < 0` are free, there
being no nonzero morphism from a sheaf in degree zero into an object in positive degrees at all.

That dévissage carries a second hypothesis, the *heart-level bridge* `hu`: that the central
elements cutting out the restricting subcategory annihilate, on the heart, by one power `Iᴺ`. It
is **not** a restriction on the site, and
`Stacks.Sites.homProVanishing_idealPowTower_singleFunctor_of_isGE_of_isLE_of_locally_span`
discharges it below, at the generality of an arbitrary site, for the central elements given by
multiplication by global sections of `O` (`Stacks.Sites.globalSectionDerivedCenter`), whenever
`Iᴺ` is locally generated by global sections. What is then left is `hneg` alone.

## The argument

The content is a multiplication: a morphism `φ : Iᵏ ⟶ F` kills `Iᴺ⁺ᵏ`, because a section of
`Iᴺ⁺ᵏ` is, locally, a sum of products `u · v` with `u` a section of `Iᴺ` and `v` a section of
`Iᵏ`, and `φ (u · v) = u · φ v` lies in `Iᴺ F = 0`. So the transition map from level `N + m` to
level `m` annihilates every morphism out of level `m` outright, rather than merely eventually.

Two things make this longer than the one line it is over a ring. The powers of a sheaf of ideals
are *sheafified* objectwise powers (`Stacks.Sites.idealPow`), so a section of `Iᴺ⁺ᵏ` is only
locally such a sum; the local description
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.mem_sheafifySubmodule_iff` supplies a covering sieve along which it is
one, and separatedness of `F` upgrades the resulting local vanishing to a global one. And the
decomposition into products is read off inside the module of sections over a single object, where
`Ideal.mul_le` applies to the ordinary ideal product `I(U)ᴺ · I(U)ᵏ`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Sites.idealPowTower` — the inverse system `m ↦ Iᵐ⁺¹` of positive powers of a sheaf of
  ideals, with the inclusions as transition maps.
* `Stacks.Sites.globalSectionDerivedCenter` — multiplication by a global section of `O`, as a
  central element of `D(O)`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Sites.idealPowTower_map` — the transition map of the tower along `n ≤ m` is the
  inclusion `Iᵐ⁺¹ ⊆ Iⁿ⁺¹`.
* `Stacks.Sites.homOfLE_comp_eq_zero_of_smul_eq_zero` — a morphism `Iⁿ⁺¹ ⟶ F` out of a power of
  a sheaf of ideals into a sheaf of modules killed by `Iᴺ` vanishes on `Iᵏ` for every
  `k ≥ N + n + 1`.
* `Stacks.Sites.homProVanishing_idealPowTower` — the morphisms out of the tower of powers into a
  sheaf killed by `Iᴺ` pro-vanish.
* `Stacks.Sites.homProVanishing_idealPowTower_singleFunctor` — the same in the derived category,
  for the tower and the target both placed in degree zero.
* `Stacks.Sites.homProVanishing_idealPowTower_singleFunctor_of_isGE_of_isLE` — the dévissage of a
  target with bounded cohomology, annihilated by a family of central elements, to the higher
  `Ext` and the heart-level bridge: the degree-zero piece is the base case above and the positive
  degrees are free.
* `Stacks.Sites.smul_eq_zero_of_locally_mem_span` — a section lying locally in the ideal spanned
  by global sections which annihilate a sheaf of modules annihilates that sheaf.
* `Stacks.Sites.globalSectionDerivedCenter_app_singleFunctor` — the central element of a global
  section acts on a sheaf of modules placed in a single degree by multiplication on that sheaf.
* `Stacks.Sites.smul_eq_zero_of_globalSectionDerivedCenter_app_eq_zero` — a global section whose
  central element kills a sheaf of modules placed in degree zero kills it sectionwise.
* `Stacks.Sites.homProVanishing_idealPowTower_singleFunctor_of_isGE_of_isLE_of_locally_span` —
  the same dévissage with the heart-level bridge discharged, leaving only the higher `Ext`.

## Implementation notes

**Why only degree zero.** The consumer of this vanishing, the dévissage
`NoetherianAdicCompletion.homProVanishing_of_isGE_of_isLE_of_mem`, asks for pro-vanishing into
every object of the restricting subcategory concentrated in a single degree, that is for
`colim_m Ext^j(Iᵐ⁺¹, F) = 0` in every degree `j` and not only in degree zero. Of those degrees
`j < 0` are empty and `j = 0` is proved here, so what the assembly
`Stacks.Sites.homProVanishing_idealPowTower_singleFunctor_of_isGE_of_isLE` is left asking for is
`j ≥ 1`.

Over a commutative ring the higher degrees follow from the degree-zero statement and
[Stacks, Tag 0954]: the sequence `Iᵐ⁺¹ ⟶ R ⟶ R/Iᵐ⁺¹` gives
`Ext^j(Iᵐ⁺¹, F) ≅ Ext^{j+1}(R/Iᵐ⁺¹, F)` for `j ≥ 1` because `Ext^j(R, F)` vanishes there, `R`
being free, and the colimit of the right-hand side is a local cohomology module of a torsion
module, which vanishes: the Čech complex of `F` on generators of `I` is `F` in degree zero,
every localization `F_{f_i}` being zero. On a site that step is unavailable: `Ext^j(O, F)` is
`H^j(F)`, the cohomology of `F` on the site, which has no reason to vanish, and the two ends of
the long exact sequence are then not zero. The vanishing of `colim_m Ext^j(Iᵐ⁺¹, F)` for `j ≥ 1`
is therefore a statement about the cohomology of the site and not a formal consequence of the
degree-zero case; nothing below asserts it.

**What the degree-zero argument does that the higher degrees cannot.** The multiplication
argument is local — a section of `Iᴺ⁺ᵏ` is a sum of products only along a covering sieve — and
what turns the resulting *local* vanishing into a global one is that `F` is a sheaf, so a section
vanishing locally vanishes. An `Ext` class in degree `j ≥ 1` is not a section of a sheaf and is
not detected on a cover. What would replace the appeal to separatedness is the local-to-global
spectral sequence `H^p(𝓔xt^q(Iᵐ⁺¹, F)) ⇒ Ext^{p+q}(Iᵐ⁺¹, F)`, whose filtration of `Ext^j` has
`j + 1` steps: if the transition maps of the *sheaves* `𝓔xt^q(Iᵐ⁺¹, F)` were annihilated after a
number of levels not depending on `q`, then so would be the transitions on `Ext^j`, after `j + 1`
times as many — and that argument would need no finiteness hypothesis on the site, just as the
degree-zero one does not.

Such a uniform bound is what happens over a ring. For `R = k[x, y]`, `I = (x, y)` and `F` killed
by `I`, the inclusion `I² ⊆ I` lifts to the minimal free resolutions as a chain map whose
degree-one component is `(0, y)`; its entries lie in `I` because the resolutions of the powers of
the irrelevant maximal ideal are linear and the inclusion raises the generating degree by one, so
`Ext^j(I, F) → Ext^j(I², F)` is zero in every degree `j` after a single level. What a site does
not have is any way to reach that computation: the sections of `𝓔xt^q(Iᵐ⁺¹, F)` over an object
`U` are again a sheaf `Ext` over the slice site and not an `Ext` over a ring, so the local
computation never bottoms out unless the site has points. On a scheme it does, stalkwise, and the
input is then the ring-level vanishing of `colim_k Ext^j_{O_x}(Iᵏ, F_x)` — [Stacks, Tag 0954],
`Stacks.LocalCohomology.localCohomology_isHomotopyColimit_derivedHomPowers`, together with the
acyclicity of an `I`-power-torsion module for local cohomology. None of that chain — sheaf `Ext`
on a site, the local-to-global spectral sequence, a stalkwise computation — is available at the
generality this file works in, and *that*, rather than quasi-coherence, is what obstructs the
higher degrees. The restriction of the dévissage to a torsion subcategory does not help on the
quasi-coherence front either: a sheaf killed by `Iᴺ` is an arbitrary module over `O/Iᴺ`, so the
affine comparisons `AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineOpen.derivedSectionsSpecIso` and [Stacks, Tag 06Z0]
do not apply to the single-degree objects the dévissage produces.

**Why the bound is `N + m` and not merely some later level.**
`NoetherianAdicCompletion.HomProVanishing` only asks for the existence of a level at which the
transition map kills the morphism. Here the level is explicit and uniform: the multiplication
argument gives level `N + m` for every morphism out of level `m` at once.
`Stacks.Sites.homOfLE_comp_eq_zero_of_smul_eq_zero` records that sharper form, and the
pro-vanishing is read off from it.

**Why the hypothesis is a single exponent `N` and not `I`-power-torsion.** The torsion condition
that the ringed-site tree carries,
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.DerivedPowerTorsion`, says the derived localizations of an object
at the generators of `I` vanish, which on cohomology sheaves says every section is killed by
*some* power of `I` and not by one power uniformly; a sheaf that is `I`-power-torsion in that
sense is a union of the subsheaves killed by the `Iᴺ`, and a single `N` for all of it needs a
finiteness hypothesis. The multiplication argument needs the uniform `N`, so that is what is
asked for here. Where this vanishing is wanted — at `E = R𝑆heafHom(V, X)` for `V` a dual Koszul
complex on a powered sequence — the uniform exponent is available: the ideal generated by the
`f_i`-powers annihilates the identity of `V`, hence every cohomology sheaf of `E`, and a power of
`I` lies in that ideal.

**The heart-level bridge needs no hypothesis on the site.** The restricting subcategory of the
dévissage is the uniform annihilation `Q Z : ∀ i, (u i).app Z = 0` by a family of natural
endomorphisms of `𝟭 D(O)`, while the base case asks for annihilation by a power `Iᴺ` of the sheaf
of ideals; bridging the two needs central elements of `D(O)` built from sections of `O`. Those are
available at this generality, and no global-sections ring, no `Linear` structure on `D(O)` and no
terminal object in the site are needed to build them:

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.globalSectionToEnd` multiplies every sheaf of `O`-modules by a
  *compatible family of local sections* of `O`, which is the right notion of a global section on
  a site with no terminal object, and is natural in the module because morphisms of sheaves of
  modules are `O`-linear;
* `CategoryTheory.CatCenter.homologicalComplex` carries that natural endomorphism to the
  complexes degreewise, and `CategoryTheory.CatCenter.localization` descends it to `D(O)`. Both
  ask only that the categories be preadditive and the second functor be a localization; the
  `R`-algebra refinements `CategoryTheory.CatCenter.homologicalComplexAlgHom` and
  `CategoryTheory.CatCenter.localizationAlgHom`, which do ask for `Linear R`, are not used.

What the bridge does need is that `Iᴺ` be *locally* generated by global sections: the central
elements see only global data, whereas `Stacks.Sites.idealPow` is a sheafified objectwise power.
That is the hypothesis `hspan` of
`Stacks.Sites.homProVanishing_idealPowTower_singleFunctor_of_isGE_of_isLE_of_locally_span`. In the
application `I` is the sheaf of ideals generated by finitely many global sections `f_1, …, f_r`,
and the spanning family is then the family of monomials of degree `N` in them: a section of `Iᴺ`
lies locally in the objectwise power `I(U)ᴺ`, each factor of a product there lies locally in the
objectwise span of the `f_i`, and the two localizations compose because a covering sieve of a
covering sieve is covering (`CategoryTheory.GrothendieckTopology.transitive`). That instantiation
is not carried out here, there being no consumer in this file's import closure. Locality itself is
harmless: separatedness of the target turns the resulting local vanishing into a global one,
exactly as in the degree-zero base case.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0942](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0942)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0954](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0954)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite AlgebraicGeometry


universe v₁ u₁ u

namespace Stacks.Sites

variable {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u})] {O : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{u}}

/-! ### The tower of positive powers -/

/-- The inverse system `m ↦ Iᵐ⁺¹` of the positive powers of a sheaf of ideals, the transition
maps being the inclusions `Iᵐ⁺¹ ⊆ Iⁿ⁺¹` for `n ≤ m`. -/
def idealPowTower (I : IdealSubsheaf O) :
    ℕᵒᵖ ⥤ _root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O) :=
  Functor.ofOpSequence (X := fun n : ℕ => (idealPow I (n + 1)).toSheafOfModules)
    fun n : ℕ => Stacks.SheafOfModules.Submodule.homOfLE
      (idealPow_antitone I (Nat.le_succ (n + 1)))

omit [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u})] in
/-- **The transition maps of the tower of powers are the inclusions.** -/
theorem idealPowTower_map (I : IdealSubsheaf O) {n m : ℕ} (h : n ≤ m) :
    (idealPowTower I).map (homOfLE h).op =
      Stacks.SheafOfModules.Submodule.homOfLE
        (idealPow_antitone I (Nat.add_le_add_right h 1)) := by
  induction m with
  | zero =>
    obtain rfl : n = 0 := Nat.le_zero.1 h
    exact (idealPowTower I).map_id _
  | succ m ih =>
    rcases Nat.eq_or_lt_of_le h with rfl | hlt
    · exact (idealPowTower I).map_id _
    · have h' : n ≤ m := Nat.lt_succ_iff.1 hlt
      rw [← NoetherianAdicCompletion.map_homOfLE_op_comp (idealPowTower I) (Nat.le_succ m) h',
        ih h', show (idealPowTower I).map (homOfLE (Nat.le_succ m)).op =
          Stacks.SheafOfModules.Submodule.homOfLE
            (idealPow_antitone I (Nat.le_succ (m + 1))) from
          Functor.ofOpSequence_map_homOfLE_succ _ m]
      exact Stacks.SheafOfModules.Submodule.homOfLE_comp_homOfLE _ _

/-! ### The multiplication argument -/

omit [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u})] in
/-- A morphism out of `Iⁿ⁺¹` into a sheaf of modules killed by `Iᴺ` annihilates every section
that lies in the objectwise power `I(U)^(N + (n + 1))`.

The sections of `Iⁿ⁺¹` over `U` form an ideal `V` of `O(U)`, the morphism is an `O(U)`-linear map
out of `V`, and the ideal product `I(U)ᴺ · I(U)ⁿ⁺¹` is spanned by the products `u * v`, each of
which is the image of the scalar multiple `u • v` of a section `v` of `V`; the hypothesis sends
`u • φ v` to zero. -/
private theorem app_eq_zero_of_mem_pow (I : IdealSubsheaf O)
    {F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O)} {N : ℕ}
    (hF : ∀ (U : Cᵒᵖ) (a : (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O).obj.obj U),
      a ∈ (idealPow I N).obj U → ∀ y : F.val.obj U, a • y = 0)
    {n : ℕ} (φ : (idealPow I (n + 1)).toSheafOfModules ⟶ F) (U : Cᵒᵖ)
    {b : (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O).obj.obj U}
    (hb : b ∈ sectionIdeal I U ^ (N + (n + 1)))
    (hb' : b ∈ (idealPow I (n + 1)).obj U) :
    PresheafOfModules.Hom.app φ.val U ⟨b, hb'⟩ = 0 := by
  have key : sectionIdeal I U ^ (N + (n + 1)) ≤
      Submodule.map ((idealPow I (n + 1)).obj U).subtype
        (LinearMap.ker (PresheafOfModules.Hom.app φ.val U).hom) := by
    rw [pow_add]
    refine Ideal.mul_le.2 fun u hu v hv => ?_
    have hv' : v ∈ (idealPow I (n + 1)).obj U := mem_idealPow_of_mem_pow I (n + 1) hv
    have hsm := LinearMap.map_smul (PresheafOfModules.Hom.app φ.val U).hom u
      (⟨v, hv'⟩ : ((idealPow I (n + 1)).obj U))
    exact ⟨_, LinearMap.mem_ker.2
      (hsm.trans (hF U u (mem_idealPow_of_mem_pow I N hu) _)), rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨y, hy, hyb⟩ := key hb
  have hxy : (⟨b, hb'⟩ : ((idealPow I (n + 1)).obj U)) = y := Subtype.ext hyb.symm
  rw [hxy]
  exact LinearMap.mem_ker.1 hy

omit [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u})] in
/-- **A morphism out of a power of a sheaf of ideals vanishes on a sufficiently higher power.**
If `F` is killed by `Iᴺ` and `k ≥ N + n + 1`, every morphism `Iⁿ⁺¹ ⟶ F` becomes zero after
precomposition with the inclusion `Iᵏ ⊆ Iⁿ⁺¹`.

A section of `Iᵏ` lies in the objectwise power `I(U)^k` along a covering sieve, hence in
`I(U)^(N + (n + 1))` there, so its image is locally zero; `F` is separated, so it is zero. -/
theorem homOfLE_comp_eq_zero_of_smul_eq_zero (I : IdealSubsheaf O)
    {F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O)} {N : ℕ}
    (hF : ∀ (U : Cᵒᵖ) (a : (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O).obj.obj U),
      a ∈ (idealPow I N).obj U → ∀ y : F.val.obj U, a • y = 0)
    {n k : ℕ} (hk : N + (n + 1) ≤ k) (hle : idealPow I k ≤ idealPow I (n + 1))
    (φ : (idealPow I (n + 1)).toSheafOfModules ⟶ F) :
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.Submodule.homOfLE hle ≫ φ = 0 := by
  ext X x
  obtain ⟨X⟩ := X
  obtain ⟨S, hS, hx⟩ := Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_sieve_of_mem_sheafifySubmodule
    (N := presheafIdealPow I k) (M := _root_.SheafOfModules.unit _) x.2
  refine F.isSheaf.isSeparated X _ hS _ 0 fun Y f hf => ?_
  rw [map_zero]
  change F.val.map f.op (PresheafOfModules.Hom.app
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Submodule.homOfLE hle ≫ φ).val (op X) x) = 0
  rw [← PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Submodule.homOfLE hle ≫ φ).val f.op x]
  exact app_eq_zero_of_mem_pow I hF φ (op Y) (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right hk (hx f hf)) _

/-! ### Pro-vanishing -/

omit [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u})] in
/-- **The morphisms out of the tower of powers of a sheaf of ideals into a sheaf killed by `Iᴺ`
pro-vanish.** The level at which a morphism out of level `n` dies is `N + n`, uniformly in the
morphism; this is `Stacks.Sites.homOfLE_comp_eq_zero_of_smul_eq_zero` read along
`Stacks.Sites.idealPowTower_map`. -/
theorem homProVanishing_idealPowTower (I : IdealSubsheaf O)
    (F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O)) (N : ℕ)
    (hF : ∀ (U : Cᵒᵖ) (a : (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O).obj.obj U),
      a ∈ (idealPow I N).obj U → ∀ y : F.val.obj U, a • y = 0) :
    NoetherianAdicCompletion.HomProVanishing (idealPowTower I) F := by
  intro n φ
  refine ⟨N + n, Nat.le_add_left n N, ?_⟩
  rw [idealPowTower_map I (Nat.le_add_left n N)]
  exact homOfLE_comp_eq_zero_of_smul_eq_zero I hF (le_refl (N + (n + 1))) _ φ

/-! ### Annihilation by a family of global sections -/

omit [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u})] in
/-- **A section lying locally in the ideal spanned by global sections which annihilate a sheaf of
modules annihilates that sheaf.** The `g i` are compatible families of local sections of `O` — the
sections of `O` over the whole site — each killing every local section of `F`; the conclusion is
that a section `a` of `O` over `U` which becomes an `O`-linear combination of the values of the
`g i` along every arrow of a covering sieve kills every section of `F` over `U`.

Locality is absorbed by separatedness of `F`, exactly as in
`Stacks.Sites.homOfLE_comp_eq_zero_of_smul_eq_zero`: the section `a • y` restricts to
`(a|_W) • (y|_W)`, which vanishes because `a|_W` lies in an ideal annihilating `F(W)`. -/
theorem smul_eq_zero_of_locally_mem_span {ι : Type*}
    (g : ι →
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O).obj ⋙ CategoryTheory.forget RingCat.{u}).sections)
    {F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O)}
    (hg : ∀ (i : ι) (V : Cᵒᵖ) (z : F.val.obj V), (g i).val V • z = 0)
    {U : Cᵒᵖ} {r : (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O).obj.obj U} {S : Sieve U.unop}
    (hS : S ∈ J U.unop)
    (hr : ∀ ⦃W : C⦄ (h : W ⟶ U.unop), S h →
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O).obj.map h.op r ∈
        Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => (g i).val (op W)))
    (y : F.val.obj U) : r • y = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨U⟩ := U
  refine F.isSheaf.isSeparated U S hS (r • y) 0 fun W h hh => ?_
  change F.val.map h.op (r • y) = F.val.map h.op (0 : F.val.obj (op U))
  rw [F.val.map_smul, map_zero]
  refine Submodule.span_induction (mem := ?_) (zero := ?_) (add := ?_) (smul := ?_) (hr h hh)
  · rintro _ ⟨i, rfl⟩
    exact hg i _ _
  · exact zero_smul _ _
  · intro x z _ _ hx hz
    rw [add_smul, hx, hz, add_zero]
  · intro c x _ hx
    rw [smul_eq_mul, mul_smul, hx, smul_zero]

section Derived

variable [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

omit [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u})] in
/-- **The derived form of the pro-vanishing, in degree zero.** The tower of powers of a sheaf of
ideals and a sheaf of modules killed by `Iᴺ` both placed in degree zero, the morphisms out of the
tower into the target pro-vanish in `D(O)`.

`CategoryTheory.DerivedCategory.singleFunctor` is fully faithful, so a morphism between objects
in degree zero is a morphism of sheaves of modules and vanishes exactly when that one does. -/
theorem homProVanishing_idealPowTower_singleFunctor (I : IdealSubsheaf O)
    (F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O)) (N : ℕ)
    (hF : ∀ (U : Cᵒᵖ) (a : (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O).obj.obj U),
      a ∈ (idealPow I N).obj U → ∀ y : F.val.obj U, a • y = 0) :
    NoetherianAdicCompletion.HomProVanishing
      (idealPowTower I ⋙
        DerivedCategory.singleFunctor
          (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O)) 0)
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor
        (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O)) 0).obj F) := by
  intro n x
  obtain ⟨φ, rfl⟩ := (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor
    (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O)) 0).map_surjective x
  obtain ⟨m, h, hφ⟩ := homProVanishing_idealPowTower I F N hF n φ
  exact ⟨m, h, by rw [Functor.comp_map, ← Functor.map_comp, hφ, Functor.map_zero]⟩

/-! ### Central elements of `D(O)` from global sections -/

/-- **Multiplication by a global section of `O`, as a central element of `D(O)`.** A compatible
family of local sections of `O` multiplies every sheaf of modules
(`Stacks.SheafOfModules.globalSectionToEnd`), hence every complex of them degreewise
(`CategoryTheory.CatCenter.homologicalComplex`), and that central element of the category of
complexes descends to the localization (`CategoryTheory.CatCenter.localization`). -/
def globalSectionDerivedCenter
    (g : ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O).obj ⋙
      CategoryTheory.forget RingCat.{u}).sections) :
    CatCenter
      (DerivedCategory (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O))) :=
  (CatCenter.homologicalComplex (ComplexShape.up ℤ)
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.globalSectionToEnd (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O)
      g)).localization
      DerivedCategory.Q (HomologicalComplex.quasiIso _ (ComplexShape.up ℤ))

omit [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u})] in
/-- **The central element acts on a sheaf of modules placed in a single degree by multiplication
on that sheaf.** The degreewise action of a central element on a complex concentrated in one
degree is the single-degree complex of its action
(`CategoryTheory.CatCenter.homologicalComplex_app_single`), and the localized central element is
computed on the image of the localization functor by that functor
(`CategoryTheory.CatCenter.localization_app`). -/
theorem globalSectionDerivedCenter_app_singleFunctor
    (g : ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O).obj ⋙
      CategoryTheory.forget RingCat.{u}).sections) (n : ℤ)
    (F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O)) :
    (globalSectionDerivedCenter g).app
        ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor
          (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O)) n).obj F) =
      (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor
        (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O)) n).map
          ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.globalSectionToEnd
            (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O) g).asHom.app F) := by
  change ((CatCenter.homologicalComplex (ComplexShape.up ℤ)
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.globalSectionToEnd (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O)
        g)).localization _ _).app
        (DerivedCategory.Q.obj ((HomologicalComplex.single
          (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O))
            (ComplexShape.up ℤ) n).obj F)) =
      DerivedCategory.Q.map ((HomologicalComplex.single
        (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O))
          (ComplexShape.up ℤ) n).map
          ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.globalSectionToEnd
            (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O) g).asHom.app F))
  rw [CatCenter.localization_app, CatCenter.homologicalComplex_app_single]

omit [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u})] in
/-- **A global section whose central element kills a sheaf of modules placed in degree zero kills
that sheaf sectionwise.** `CategoryTheory.DerivedCategory.singleFunctor` is faithful, so the
vanishing in `D(O)` is the vanishing of multiplication by the section on `F`, which is tested on
local sections. -/
theorem smul_eq_zero_of_globalSectionDerivedCenter_app_eq_zero
    (g : ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O).obj ⋙
      CategoryTheory.forget RingCat.{u}).sections)
    {F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O)}
    (h : (globalSectionDerivedCenter g).app
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor
        (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O)) 0).obj F) = 0)
    (U : Cᵒᵖ) (y : F.val.obj U) : g.val U • y = 0 := by
  have h0 : (Stacks.SheafOfModules.globalSectionToEnd
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O) g).asHom.app F = 0 :=
    (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor
      (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O)) 0).map_injective
        (((globalSectionDerivedCenter_app_singleFunctor g 0 F).symm.trans h).trans
          (Functor.map_zero _ _ _).symm)
  have hap := Stacks.SheafOfModules.globalSectionToEnd_apply
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O) g F U y
  rw [h0] at hap
  exact hap.symm

omit [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u})] in
/-- **The dévissage fed by the degree-zero base case: what remains is the higher `Ext`.** Let
`u : ι → (𝟭 D ⟶ 𝟭 D)` be a family of central elements of `D = D(O)` — multiplication by global
scalars, in the application — and let `E` be an object with bounded cohomology annihilated by all
of them. Then the morphisms out of the tower of powers of `ℐ` pro-vanish into `E` as soon as they
pro-vanish into the single-degree objects of that subcategory in the **negative** degrees.

Three things are being combined, and the hypotheses that remain are exactly the ones that are not
available.

* The restricting subcategory is the uniform annihilation `Q Z : ∀ i, (u i).app Z = 0`, which the
  canonical truncations preserve
  (`NoetherianAdicCompletion.app_truncLT_eq_zero_of_app_eq_zero` and its companion), so the
  dévissage `NoetherianAdicCompletion.homProVanishing_of_isGE_of_isLE_of_mem_of_isLE` applies and
  reduces `E` to its single-degree pieces inside `Q`.
* The tower sits in degree zero, so the single-degree objects in degrees `≥ 1` carry no nonzero
  morphism out of the tower at all and need nothing supplied.
* In degree `0` a single-degree object is `(DerivedCategory.singleFunctor _ 0).obj F` for a sheaf
  of modules `F` (`DerivedCategory.exists_iso_singleFunctor_obj_of_isGE_of_isLE`), and
  `Stacks.Sites.homProVanishing_idealPowTower_singleFunctor` discharges it — provided `F` is
  killed by one power `ℐᴺ`. That is what `hu` asks: that the annihilation condition cutting `Q`
  out implies, on the heart, annihilation by `ℐᴺ`. For `u` the family of multiplications by
  global sections spanning `ℐᴺ` locally it holds, by separatedness of `F`; that is
  `Stacks.Sites.homProVanishing_idealPowTower_singleFunctor_of_isGE_of_isLE_of_locally_span`,
  which supplies `hu` rather than assuming it.

What is left is `hneg`, the single-degree hypothesis in the degrees `n < 0`, that is
`colim_m Ext^j(ℐᵐ⁺¹, F) = 0` for `j = -n ≥ 1` and `F` killed by `ℐᴺ`. It is not supplied here and
is not a formal consequence of the degree-zero case; see the implementation notes. -/
theorem homProVanishing_idealPowTower_singleFunctor_of_isGE_of_isLE
    (I : IdealSubsheaf O) (N : ℕ) {ι : Type*}
    (u : ι →
      (𝟭 (DerivedCategory (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O))) ⟶
      𝟭 (DerivedCategory (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O)))))
    (hu : ∀ F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O),
      (∀ i, (u i).app ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor
          (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O)) 0).obj F) = 0) →
      ∀ (U : Cᵒᵖ) (a : (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O).obj.obj U),
        a ∈ (idealPow I N).obj U → ∀ y : F.val.obj U, a • y = 0)
    (hneg : ∀ n : ℤ, n < 0 →
      ∀ Z : DerivedCategory (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O)),
        DerivedCategory.TStructure.t.IsLE Z n → DerivedCategory.TStructure.t.IsGE Z n →
        (∀ i, (u i).app Z = 0) →
        NoetherianAdicCompletion.HomProVanishing (idealPowTower I ⋙
          DerivedCategory.singleFunctor
            (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O)) 0) Z)
    (E : DerivedCategory (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O)))
    (a b : ℤ)
    (hGE : DerivedCategory.TStructure.t.IsGE E a)
    (hLE : DerivedCategory.TStructure.t.IsLE E b)
    (hE : ∀ i, (u i).app E = 0) :
    NoetherianAdicCompletion.HomProVanishing (idealPowTower I ⋙
      DerivedCategory.singleFunctor
        (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O)) 0) E := by
  refine NoetherianAdicCompletion.homProVanishing_of_isGE_of_isLE_of_mem_of_isLE
    DerivedCategory.TStructure.t _ (fun Z => ∀ i, (u i).app Z = 0) 0
    (fun m => inferInstanceAs (DerivedCategory.TStructure.t.IsLE
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor
        (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O)) 0).obj
          ((idealPowTower I).obj (op m))) 0))
    (fun n X hX i => NoetherianAdicCompletion.app_truncLT_eq_zero_of_app_eq_zero
      DerivedCategory.TStructure.t (u i) n X (hX i))
    (fun n X hX i => NoetherianAdicCompletion.app_truncGE_eq_zero_of_app_eq_zero
      DerivedCategory.TStructure.t (u i) n X (hX i))
    ?_ E a b hGE hLE hE
  intro n hn Z hZLE hZGE hQZ
  rcases lt_or_eq_of_le hn with hlt | rfl
  · exact hneg n hlt Z hZLE hZGE hQZ
  · have := hZLE
    have := hZGE
    obtain ⟨F, ⟨e⟩⟩ := DerivedCategory.exists_iso_singleFunctor_obj_of_isGE_of_isLE Z 0
    refine (homProVanishing_idealPowTower_singleFunctor I F N (hu F fun i => ?_)).of_iso e.symm
    have h := (u i).naturality e.inv
    simp only [Functor.id_obj, Functor.id_map] at h
    rw [← cancel_mono e.inv, ← h, hQZ i, comp_zero, zero_comp]

omit [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u})] in
/-- **The dévissage with the heart-level bridge supplied: only the negative degrees remain.**
This is `Stacks.Sites.homProVanishing_idealPowTower_singleFunctor_of_isGE_of_isLE` with its
hypothesis `hu` discharged, for the family of central elements given by multiplication by global
sections of `O`.

The input is a family `g` of global sections of `O` — compatible families of local sections, so no
terminal object in the site is needed — which spans `ℐᴺ` locally, in the sense that every section
of `ℐᴺ` becomes an `O`-linear combination of the values of the `g i` along the arrows of some
covering sieve. Then multiplication by `g i` is a central element of `D(O)`
(`Stacks.Sites.globalSectionDerivedCenter`), its vanishing on a sheaf of modules placed in degree
zero is the sectionwise vanishing of multiplication by `g i`
(`Stacks.Sites.smul_eq_zero_of_globalSectionDerivedCenter_app_eq_zero`, by faithfulness of the
single-degree functor), and the spanning hypothesis propagates that to annihilation by every
section of `ℐᴺ` (`Stacks.Sites.smul_eq_zero_of_locally_mem_span`, by separatedness of the target).

So `hu` was never a restriction on the site: it is available at the generality of an arbitrary
site, for any sheaf of ideals whose `N`-th power is locally generated by global sections. In the
application `ℐ` is generated by finitely many global sections and the `g i` are the monomials of
degree `N` in them; see the implementation notes. What remains is `hneg`, the single-degree
hypothesis in the negative degrees, `colim_m Ext^j(ℐᵐ⁺¹, F) = 0` for `j ≥ 1`; see the
implementation notes for why that one is not a formal consequence of the degree-zero case. -/
theorem homProVanishing_idealPowTower_singleFunctor_of_isGE_of_isLE_of_locally_span
    (I : IdealSubsheaf O) (N : ℕ) {ι : Type*}
    (g : ι →
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O).obj ⋙ CategoryTheory.forget RingCat.{u}).sections)
    (hspan : ∀ (U : Cᵒᵖ) (r : (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O).obj.obj U),
      r ∈ (idealPow I N).obj U → ∃ S : Sieve U.unop, S ∈ J U.unop ∧
        ∀ ⦃W : C⦄ (h : W ⟶ U.unop), S h →
          (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O).obj.map h.op r ∈
            Ideal.span (Set.range fun i => (g i).val (op W)))
    (hneg : ∀ n : ℤ, n < 0 →
      ∀ Z : DerivedCategory (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O)),
        DerivedCategory.TStructure.t.IsLE Z n → DerivedCategory.TStructure.t.IsGE Z n →
        (∀ i, (globalSectionDerivedCenter (g i)).app Z = 0) →
        NoetherianAdicCompletion.HomProVanishing (idealPowTower I ⋙
          DerivedCategory.singleFunctor
            (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O)) 0) Z)
    (E : DerivedCategory (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O)))
    (a b : ℤ)
    (hGE : DerivedCategory.TStructure.t.IsGE E a)
    (hLE : DerivedCategory.TStructure.t.IsLE E b)
    (hE : ∀ i, (globalSectionDerivedCenter (g i)).app E = 0) :
    NoetherianAdicCompletion.HomProVanishing (idealPowTower I ⋙
      DerivedCategory.singleFunctor
        (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf O)) 0) E :=
  homProVanishing_idealPowTower_singleFunctor_of_isGE_of_isLE I N
    (fun i => (globalSectionDerivedCenter (g i)).asHom)
    (fun _ hF U r hr y => by
      obtain ⟨S, hS, hmem⟩ := hspan U r hr
      exact smul_eq_zero_of_locally_mem_span g
        (fun i => smul_eq_zero_of_globalSectionDerivedCenter_app_eq_zero (g i) (hF i)) hS hmem y)
    hneg E a b hGE hLE hE

end Derived

end Stacks.Sites

end
